    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0729" n="1463" xml:id="pg1463"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20,
                        1896</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 804.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 755, of the 2d
                    instant, touching the situation in the province of Aleppo.</p>
                <p>The Department heartily approves your purpose to ask to have regular troops
                    detailed for the protection of American citizens at Aintab, and I observe with
                    no slight degree of satisfaction your strong commendation of the action of Mr.
                    Frederick Poche, our consular agent at Aleppo, in behalf of our citizens there.
                    It is most cordially appreciated by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
